{title: Two Small Coins}
{subtitle: Mark 12:41–44}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]rich men came in their fine clothes [Eb]
Their purses hea[F]vy, their noses [Bb]high
They dropped their [Gm7]silver in the treasury [Eb]
And made sure [Cm]everyone saw it [F]fly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Then came a widow, thin and [Bb]gray [F/A]
[Gm]Two copper coins in her worn [Eb]hand
[Cm]She dropped them in without a [F]sound
[Eb]And no one there would under[F]stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This [Bb]poor widow has put in more [Eb]than all the others
For [Bb]they all gave out of their [Eb]abundance
[Gm]But she, out of [F]her poverty, [Eb]put in everything [F]she owned
All she had to live [Bb]on [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Jesus sat down across the way [Eb]
[F]And watched the people as they [Bb]gave [F/A]
[Gm]He saw the coins that no [Eb]one heard
[Cm]He saw the faith that makes [F]us brave
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This poor [Bb]widow has put in more than all [Eb]the others
For they all [Bb]gave out of their abun[Eb]dance
But she, [Gm]out of her po[F]verty, put in [Eb]everything she owned
[F]All she had to live on
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Two small [Bb]coins [F/A][Gm7][F][Eb]
[F]All she had to live [Bb]on
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
